sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch11-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The permanent spiral forms found in organisms, such as the horns of ruminants, molluscan and foraminiferal shells and the arrangement of florets in the sunflower, are all logarithmic spirals; the outline of a cordate leaf is the one spiral-like organic outline that is not.";
    dc:type "mathematical-law";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Horns, molluscan shells, foraminifera and sunflower florets follow the logarithmic spiral";
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "r = a e^{\\theta \\cot\\alpha}";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XI, “The Logarithmic Spiral”; topic “Organic spirals and their classification”. Scope: ruminant horns, molluscan shells, foraminiferal shells, sunflower capitula; excludes cordate leaf outlines"
}
